From 433a38d1d6407c40df74eae8d9817ca11761d564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:44:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bundle_runtime: never start the application to check it

Reported from a real run: `bundle_runtime.py <zip> --zip` started the
application - browser, identity screen, the lot - and wrote no zip.

The check at the end of the bundling asked PM_APP.py --version, and that
option did not exist. The application ignores words it does not know, so
instead of answering it STARTED, and an application that has started does
not come back: it serves and waits for a person. subprocess.run then raised
TimeoutExpired, uncaught, and the run died before the packaging block. The
operator was left with a login page and nothing to hand out.

It got out of the door because the block sat inside `if os.name == "nt"`.
Nothing in the test suite, which runs elsewhere, could ever execute it.

  * --version is now a real option: it prints the version and returns,
    starting no server, opening no browser, touching no data folder. That
    makes it usable as "can this Python run this application" without
    running it, which is the question the bundler is actually asking.
  * The checks move into verify(exe, app), which TAKES THE INTERPRETER AS
    AN ARGUMENT. main() passes the bundled python.exe on Windows; the tests
    pass the one they are running on, anywhere. --check-with names another.
  * run_one() catches TimeoutExpired and OSError and returns them as text.
    A check that hangs is now a printed answer, not the end of the run.
  * A build with no --version in its launch.py is not asked at all, because
    asking would start it.
  * Packaging happens even when a check fails. The failure is the last
    thing said - NOT READY TO HAND OUT - and sets exit code 1, so the zip
    exists and nobody hands it out by accident.

Eight checks added to tools/test_no_python.py covering exactly this shape:
that the checks are callable from here at all, that all four return in
well under the timeout, that a hang is an answer rather than an exception,
that an older build is skipped instead of started, and that a failed check
still leaves the zip written. Full suite green (40 python + storage.mjs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015uUAZtqavUrwFq3tABxWDZ
